WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.532
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Wednesday, November fourth.

2
00:00:04.532 --> 00:00:12.108
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.108 --> 00:00:14.644
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.644 --> 00:00:31.514
Today: a wave of bomb threats against flights across Europe, drone attacks on Iranian Kurdish opposition groups in northern Iraq, a state of emergency in parts of Belize, an update on Iran and the Strait of Hormuz, and a deadly ambush on security forces in northwest Nigeria.

5
00:00:31.514 --> 00:00:32.690
We start in Europe.

6
00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:39.403
Reuters reports bomb threats against passenger flights and a cruise ship disrupted travel across Europe yesterday, and no devices were found.

7
00:00:39.403 --> 00:00:48.915
AFP puts the number of targeted flights at about ten, and says the threats forced the brief closure of a Warsaw airport and the scrambling of air force planes in Rome.

8
00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:57.103
Reuters says Warsaw Modlin airport reopened after its threat, and a second flight was checked at Warsaw Chopin.

9
00:00:57.103 --> 00:00:59.375
Turning to Iraq.

10
00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:08.611
Reuters reports, citing sources, that drones attacked Iranian Kurdish opposition groups in Sulaymaniyah and east of Erbil, in the Kurdistan region, overnight.

11
00:01:08.611 --> 00:01:09.111
Next, Belize.

12
00:01:09.111 --> 00:01:21.844
Canada updated its Belize travel advice to add a thirty day state of emergency declared on Saturday, October thirty first, in parts of Belize City, Belize District and Cayo District, following a sharp rise in violent crime.

13
00:01:21.844 --> 00:01:34.862
Canada says security forces there can restrict movement, conduct searches and detain people, and advises travelers in those areas to expect more police and military, carry identification and plan for transport delays.

14
00:01:34.862 --> 00:01:42.981
Canada's overall level is unchanged: exercise a high degree of caution, and avoid non essential travel to Southside Belize City.

15
00:01:42.981 --> 00:01:44.550
An update on Iran.

16
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:53.627
The Institute for the Study of War and Critical Threats assess that Iranian forces attempted to shoot down a U.S. aircraft near Qeshm Island, in the Strait of Hormuz, on Monday, November second.

17
00:01:53.627 --> 00:01:55.407
And in Nigeria.

18
00:01:55.407 --> 00:02:10.982
Reuters, citing local security officials, reports at least eight people were killed when gunmen ambushed a convoy carrying security personnel near Gidan Giye in the Tsafe area of Zamfara State yesterday, including five police officers and three members of a state protection guard.

19
00:02:10.982 --> 00:02:16.936
The terrorism tracker TRAC attributes the attack to a bandit group and says several others were kidnapped.

20
00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:21.391
Now a few quick notes by region.

21
00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:27.843
In the Middle East, Reuters reports Syria says it foiled a Hezbollah plot to attack the oil refinery in Homs.

22
00:02:27.843 --> 00:02:34.748
The Long War Journal reports Lebanon's military prosecutor charged thirteen people over a Hezbollah explosives shipment.

23
00:02:34.748 --> 00:02:44.718
In Europe, the Institute for the Study of War reports Russia carried out a large combined drone and missile strike on Ukrainian energy infrastructure overnight Sunday into Monday.

24
00:02:44.718 --> 00:02:57.896
Reuters reports the Russian held Zaporizhzhia nuclear plant says a Ukrainian drone killed two people, including a station employee, and that Latvia believes one of two drones that entered its airspace was Russian and the other Ukrainian.

25
00:02:57.896 --> 00:03:09.270
In Northern Ireland, the Belfast Telegraph reports police said a large haul of explosive devices found in Belfast's Shankill Road area over the weekend is linked to extreme far right terrorism.

26
00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:21.917
In Africa, Critical Threats says two conflict trackers and an Ethiopian government aligned official alleged that Ethiopian and Eritrean forces exchanged fire on their shared border, though it could not confirm the claims.

27
00:03:21.917 --> 00:03:27.346
B B C Africa reports Uganda arrested former deputy military chief Peter Elwelu over alleged activities aimed at destabilizing the country.

28
00:03:27.346 --> 00:03:40.028
And the U.N. humanitarian office says El Niño floods are hitting Somalia, with some three point four million people possibly at risk of flooding by the end of the year.

29
00:03:40.028 --> 00:03:46.545
In South Asia, Pakistan's A R Y News reports police in Lakki Marwat, in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, killed two militants, including a suicide bomber.

30
00:03:46.545 --> 00:04:01.769
In health, the C D C's rule requiring everyone boarding a flight to the United States to attest they have not been in the Democratic Republic of the Congo in the previous twenty one days took effect at eleven fifty nine last night, Eastern time.

31
00:04:01.769 --> 00:04:16.087
Australia says travelers to Kenya may need to complete a health declaration and undergo screening on arrival because of the Ebola outbreak, and the U.K. updated its Madagascar advice with Ebola entry requirements and health screening.

32
00:04:16.087 --> 00:04:26.330
And in cyber, Microsoft says it has identified a fake download campaign that targets people searching for cracked software, free games and plugins with trojanized installers.

33
00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:36.897
In an update on the Binance theft, Reuters reports the exchange says hackers used a bogus job interview and software hidden in an advertisement to compromise its engineers' computers.

34
00:04:36.897 --> 00:04:38.314
That's today's brief.

35
00:04:38.314 --> 00:04:46.671
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

36
00:04:46.671 --> 00:04:54.920
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

37
00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.003
This brief is digitally narrated.

38
00:04:57.003 --> 00:04:57.911
Questions?

39
00:04:57.911 --> 00:05:01.325
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

40
00:05:01.325 --> 00:05:03.362
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
